                  %a{:href => "#group_actions"} Group actions
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            There are various variants of the notion of something
            %em acting
            on something else. They are all closely related.
          %p
            The simplest concept of an action involves one
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            and such an action is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  act\colon X \times Y \to Y
                  \\,.
          %p
            For fixed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            this produces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunction"} endofunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act(x,-) \colon Y \to Y
            and hence some “transformation” or “action” on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            acts on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x\mapsto act(x,-))
            is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} curried
            function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi act
                    %mo ^
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{act}\colon X \to Y^Y
            of the original
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi act
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctions"} endofunctions
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            Usually the key aspect of an action of some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            itself carries an algebraic structure, such as being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            (or just a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            or an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^Y
            and preserved by the curried action
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi act
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{act}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is any set then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^Y
            is a monoid, and when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            acts on it one calls it an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSet"} X-set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^Y
            to have a ring/algebra structure,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            must be some sort of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            with the action by
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functions"} linear functions
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
          %p
            In terms of the uncurried action
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times Y\to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the same as first multiplying them and then acting with the result:
          #eq:ActionProperty.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  act(x_2,act(x_1,y)) = act(x_2\cdot x_1, y)
                  \\,.
          %p
            To be precise, this is the condition for a
            = succeed ";" do
              %em left action
            %em right action
            is defined dually in terms of a map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\times X\to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has no algebraic structure, or if its relevant structure is commutative, then there is no essential difference between the two; but in general they can be quite different.
          %p
            This
            %em action property
            can also often be identified with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            property: it characterizes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}X
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            (such as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is an object. The distinction between left and right actions is mirrored in the variance; acting on the left yields a covariant functor, whereas acting on the right is expressed via contravariance.
          %p
            In this way essentially every kind of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-functor"} n-functor
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            may be thought of as defining a generalized kind of action. This perspective on actions is particularly prevalent in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            may be thought of as producing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
            of actions in this general functorial sense.
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            (or one of its variants), this perspective turns into the perspective where an action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y/X
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            is
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y/X
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the total space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y/X
            of this bundle is typically the “weak”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            (for instance:
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}X
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y/X \to \mathbf{B}X
            is the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            via the action to this universal bundle. For more on this perspective on actions see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#ActionsOfAGroup Actions of a group
          %p
            An
            %strong action
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon G \to Aut(S)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(S)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            Group actions, especially
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
            actions on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %em transformation groups
            (starting around
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Klein1872"} Klein 1872, Sec. 1
            %a{:href => "#Koszul65"} Koszul 65
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Bredon72"} Bredon 72
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#tomDieck79"} tom Dieck 79
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#tomDieck87"} tom Dieck 87
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            that acts is understood, one calls (
            %a{:href => "#Bredon72"}> Bredon 72, Ch. II
            ) the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with an action by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} topological G-space
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifold"} G-manifold
          %p
            As indicated above, a more abstract but equivalent definition regards the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as a category (a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            %em action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho \colon \mathbf{B} G \to \mathcal{C}
          %p
            Here the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of the previous definition is the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(\ast)
            of that single object.
          %p
            Concretely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a category like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo ×
                          %mi S
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo ,
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  G \times S &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; S
                  \\\
                  (g,s) &amp;\mapsto&amp; \rho(g)(s)
                  }
          %p
            which satisfies the
            %em action property
          #eq:ActionPropertyOfGroupActions.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{
                  g_1, g_2, s
                  }{\forall}
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\rho(g_1 \cdot g_2)(s)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\rho(g_1)
                  \\big(
                  \\rho(g_2)(s)
                  \\big)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{s}{\forall}
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\rho(e)(s) \;=\; s
          %h3#actions_of_a_monoid Actions of a monoid
          %p
            More generally we can define an
            %em action
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to be a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho: \mathbf{B} M \to C
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} M
            is (again)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            regarded as a one-object category.
          %p
            The
            %em category of actions
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is then defined to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{B} M}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            this is called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSet"} MSet
          %p
            Considering this in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            yields the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+objects"} action objects
          %h3#actions_of_a_category Actions of a category
          %p
            One can
            %sup#fnref:1
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            also define an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+of+a+category+on+a+set"} action of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            on the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as a functor from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          %p
            Another perspective on the same situation is: a (small) category is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in the category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+of+a+category+on+a+set"} action of a category on a set
          %p
            On the other hand, an action of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            (not
            %em in
            a monoidal category, as above) is called an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actegory"} module category
            (also “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actegory"}> actegory
            ”). This notion can be expanded of course to actions
            %em in
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+bicategory"} monoidal bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as monoidal bicategory it specializes to the notion of module category.
          %h3#actions_of_a_group_object Actions of a group object
          %p
            Suppose we have a category,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on an object,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            By the adjointness relation between cartesian product,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ?
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times ?
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ?
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ?^A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: G\to Aut(X)
          %p corresponds to a function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act: G\times X\to X
          %p
            which will have various properties encoding that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            was a homomorphism of groups:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act(g_1g_2,x) = act(g_1,act(g_2,x))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act(1,x) = x
          %p and these can be encoded diagrammatically.
          %p
            Because of this, we can
            %strong define
            an action of a group object,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on an object,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to be a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act: G\times X\to X
          %p satisfying conditions that certain diagrams (left to the reader) encoding these two rules, commute.
          %p
            The advantage of this is that it does not require the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to have internal automorphism group objects for all objects being considered.
          %p
            As an example, only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological spaces
            have well-behaved topological automorphism groups, and thus actions of topological spaces on topological spaces must either be restricted to actions on locally compact spaces, or else be defined as above.
          %p
            As another example, within the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite groups
            viewed as topological groups, not all objects have automorphism groups for which the natural topology is profinite. Thus profinite group actions on (the underlying topological space of) a profinite group must either be given in this form, or else be restricted to actions on profinite groups for which the automorphism group is naturally profinite.
          %h3#actions_of_a_monoid_object Actions of a monoid object
          %p
            Suppose we have a category,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on an object,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            By the adjointness relation between cartesian product,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ?
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times ?
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ?
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ?^A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: M\to End(X)
          %p corresponds to a function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act: M\times X\to X
          %p
            which will have various properties encoding that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            was a homomorphism of monoids:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act(m_1m_2,x) = act(m_1,act(m_2,x))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act(1,x) = x
          %p and these can be encoded diagrammatically.
          %p
            Because of this, we can
            %strong define
            an action of a monoid object,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on an object,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to be a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act:M\times X\to X
          %p satisfying conditions that certain diagrams (left to the reader) encoding these two rules, commute.
          %p
            The advantage of this is that it does not require the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to have internal endomorphism monoid objects for all objects being considered.
          %h3#actions_of_a_set Actions of a set
          %p
            The action of a set on a set was defined above; it consists of a function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi act
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act: X\times Y\to Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            as its vertices, with its edges labeled by elements of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deterministic+automaton"} deterministic automaton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            the set of states and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the set of inputs.
          %p
            That an action is a type of edge labeled quiver can be seen by explicitly giving the product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            functions,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi act
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 2
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\overset{\quad p_1 \quad}{ \leftarrow}X\times Y\underoverset{\quad act \quad}{p_2}{\rightrightarrows}Y
          %p The shape of this diagram corresponds to that of an edge labeled quiver:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Labels
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi label
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi Edges
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi target
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mi source
                  %mi Vertices
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Labels\overset{\quad label \quad}{ \leftarrow}Edges\underoverset{\quad target \quad}{source}{\rightrightarrows}Vertices
          %p
            While the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has no algebraic structure to be preserved, the action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi act
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act
            generates a unique
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
              action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi act
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act^{*}:X^{*}\times Y\to Y
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{*}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monoid"} free monoid
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            containing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path"} paths
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            elements. The monoidal structure of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^*
            is preserved: two actions in succession is equal to the action of the concatenation of their paths.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi act
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi act
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} act^{*}(x^{*}_2,act(x^{*}_1,y)) = act^{*}(x^{*}_2\cdot x^{*}_1, y)
          %p
            An action of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in itself is also called a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magma"} magma
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
                is a “linear action”.
            %li
              %p
                In
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
                one considers
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+actions"} Hamiltonian actions
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} topological G-space
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+action"} circle action
